FAQ = [
 ("What is the best tonneau cover for a Ford Maverick?",
  "For most owners, the BAKFlip MX4 448324. It has polymer-reinforced aluminum panels, a 400 lb evenly distributed rating, auto-latches, a 5-year warranty and a clamp-on install BAK puts at under 30 minutes. RealTruck lists it at $1,049.99. If you want the strongest cover for less, the UnderCover Triad is rated at 600 lb for $849.99. For a budget soft cover, the TruXedo TruXport ($349.99) and Tyger T3 ($239) both carry 5-year warranties."),
 ("Do hybrid and EcoBoost Mavericks need different tonneau covers?",
  "No. Both powertrains use the same 4.5 ft (54.4 in) FLEXBED, and every cover here is listed for the Maverick without a powertrain split. The hybrid's high-voltage battery sits under the rear-seat floor, not in the bed. Maverick owners mention this when explaining why the hybrid has slightly less rear legroom. Hybrid vs EcoBoost matters for floor liners and towing, but not for the bed cover."),
 ("How long is the Ford Maverick bed?",
  "Every 2022–2026 Maverick has a single 4.5 ft bed that measures 54.4 in long, 53.3 in wide between the sidewalls and 42.6 in between the wheel wells. Retailers label it differently: Amazon titles say 4'6\" (54.4\"), some BAK listings say 4'5\" (54\"), and RealTruck's fitment tool says 4'4\". They all mean the same bed. There is only one cab, the four-door SuperCrew, so the only thing to check is that the listing names the Maverick."),
 ("Do tonneau covers block the FLEXBED slots?",
  "No. The FLEXBED's stamped slots for 2x4 and 2x6 dividers are in the bed sidewalls below the rail, and the covers here clamp to the underside of the bed rail above them. You can still build dividers or shelves in the slots with the cover closed, provided the lumber sits below the rail line. Anything that pokes above the rails, such as a tall divider, will stop a cover from closing."),
 ("Why do Maverick tonneau covers leak?",
  "Maverick owners on MaverickTruckClub point to the bed design more than the covers. Water runs into channels in the plastic bed-rail caps and toward the bulkhead, with, as one owner put it, \"no where for water to go other than towards bed.\" The reported fixes are extra weatherstrip at the bulkhead and tailgate, butyl tape in the rail-cap channels, and larger (½ in) drain tubes. One owner with a TruXedo Lo Pro reported no more water after adding weatherstrip."),
 ("Hard or soft cover — which is better on a Maverick?",
  "Buy a hard cover if you leave tools or bags in the bed. The MX4, UnderCover Flex, Triad and RetraxPRO lock under the closed tailgate and are rated for 400 to 600 lb spread evenly. Soft covers such as the TruXport ($349.99) and Tyger T3 ($239) weigh little, clamp on in minutes and cost a quarter as much. On a compact truck, many owners want only weather and privacy, and a soft cover does that job."),
 ("Can I put cargo on top of a Maverick tonneau cover?",
  "Only on hard covers and only within the maker's evenly distributed rating: 600 lb for the UnderCover Triad, 500 lb for the RetraxPRO MX, 400 lb for the BAKFlip MX4 and UnderCover Flex. Those ratings assume a flat load spread over the panels. A heavy cooler corner or a knee concentrates the weight and can dent a panel. Soft roll-ups and tri-folds carry no rating."),
 ("Does the Tyger T3 fit every Maverick?",
  "Tyger lists the T3 TG-BC3F1061 for the 2022–2026 Maverick 4.5 ft bed but says it does \"not fit models with Utility Track System\". If your bed has aftermarket or accessory track rails along the top of the sides, pick another cover or ask Tyger. Tyger also says an over-the-rail bedliner needs small holes cut for the clamps. Under-rail and spray-in liners need nothing."),
 ("Is a retractable cover worth it on a Maverick?",
  "For most owners, no. The RetraxPRO MX 80337 is rated for 500 lb, locks at any position and carries a lifetime warranty, but at about $2,150 it costs roughly twice as much as the MX4. The canister also takes part of an already short 54.4 in bed. It makes sense if you use the Maverick as a work truck and open the bed many times a day."),
 ("Does a tonneau cover affect towing or the hitch on a Maverick?",
  "No. The cover sits on the bed rails and seals against the closed tailgate, and it doesn't touch the receiver. What does change with towing is the hitch itself. Only trucks with the 4K Tow Package get a 2 in receiver, and others have a smaller Class I. If you tow a camper, keep the tailgate closed so the rear of the cover stays locked, and check that a trailer tongue-jack handle can't swing into the tailgate."),
]

